{
  "schemaVersion": "1",
  "id": "fixture-reading-monitoring",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "reading-note",
      "family": "reading-monitoring",
      "regions": [
        {
          "id": "note-chrome",
          "kind": "tabs",
          "state": "active",
          "background": "surface",
          "foreground": "foreground",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "tab-reading",
              "kind": "tab",
              "state": "active",
              "text": "Reading",
              "foreground": "accent"
            },
            {
              "id": "tab-notes",
              "kind": "tab",
              "state": "inactive",
              "text": "Notes",
              "foreground": "text-muted"
            },
            {
              "id": "tab-archive",
              "kind": "tab",
              "state": "inactive",
              "text": "Archive",
              "foreground": "text-muted"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "prose",
          "kind": "column",
          "state": "active",
          "background": "surface",
          "foreground": "foreground",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "heading-title",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "active",
              "text": "Keeping a personal archive that lasts",
              "foreground": "accent"
            },
            {
              "id": "meta-published",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "muted",
              "text": "Published 2026-08-13 · 2 min read",
              "foreground": "text-muted"
            },
            {
              "id": "heading-why",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "active",
              "text": "Why plain text wins",
              "foreground": "accent"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-01",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "A personal archive is only as durable as the format it is stored in.",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-02",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "text": "Proprietary formats come and go, but ",
                  "state": "default",
                  "foreground": "foreground"
                },
                {
                  "text": "plain text",
                  "state": "info",
                  "foreground": "accent"
                },
                {
                  "text": " has outlived every",
                  "state": "default",
                  "foreground": "foreground"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "para-03",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "editor, every operating system, and every vendor that promised to",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-04",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "keep your notes safe. When a tool dies, its files still open in anything.",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-05",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "text": "Plain text also makes the archive searchable. Tools like ",
                  "state": "default",
                  "foreground": "foreground"
                },
                {
                  "text": "grep",
                  "state": "default",
                  "foreground": "text-secondary"
                },
                {
                  "text": " and ",
                  "state": "default",
                  "foreground": "foreground"
                },
                {
                  "text": "ripgrep",
                  "state": "default",
                  "foreground": "text-secondary"
                },
                {
                  "text": " can scan a",
                  "state": "default",
                  "foreground": "foreground"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "para-06",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "decade of notes in under a second, and the results are reproducible. A binary format",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-07",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "hides its contents behind an application; a text file shows exactly what it holds.",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-08",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "The trade-off is that plain text has no styling. Headings, links,",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-09",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "and emphasis are conventions rather than features. That is a",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-10",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "feature in disguise: the meaning lives in the words, not in the",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-11",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "rendering, so the archive survives any change of taste in how it is displayed.",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "heading-example",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "active",
              "text": "A minimal example",
              "foreground": "accent"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-12",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "A single directory with a few conventions is enough to start. Keep one file",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-13",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "per topic, name it with a date prefix, and write in short paragraphs. The",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-14",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "structure below has served well for years and needs no special tooling to read.",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "code-example",
              "kind": "code",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "archive/\n  2026-08-13-reading.md\n  2026-08-14-backups.md\n  index.md",
              "background": "surface-elevated",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-15",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "text": "The ",
                  "state": "default",
                  "foreground": "foreground"
                },
                {
                  "text": "index.md",
                  "state": "default",
                  "foreground": "text-secondary"
                },
                {
                  "text": " file is the only piece of structure that matters. It lists",
                  "state": "default",
                  "foreground": "foreground"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "para-16",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "every note with a one-line summary, so the archive can be navigated",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-17",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "without opening each file. Regenerate it with a script when it drifts out of date.",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-18",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "text": "Versioning is the second habit. A ",
                  "state": "default",
                  "foreground": "foreground"
                },
                {
                  "text": "git",
                  "state": "default",
                  "foreground": "text-secondary"
                },
                {
                  "text": " repository turns every edit",
                  "state": "default",
                  "foreground": "foreground"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "para-19",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "into a recoverable point, and a remote copy turns the archive into a",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-20",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "backup. Neither step requires the notes to be in any particular format.",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-21",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "A backup that is never tested is not a backup. Restore a single file to a clean",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-22",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "directory once a season, and confirm the index still opens. The exercise takes",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-23",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "minutes and catches the silent failures that only show up when the archive is needed most.",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "heading-breaks",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "active",
              "text": "What breaks an archive",
              "foreground": "accent"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-24",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "The archive fails in predictable ways. Files are lost to a disk that dies, a",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-25",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "sync that overwrites, or a rename that breaks a link. Each failure has a",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-26",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "cheap fix, but only if the archive is plain text and versioned from the start.",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-27",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "Links between notes are the most fragile part. A link that names a file",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-28",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "by its full path breaks the moment the file moves. Prefer links that",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-29",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "text": "name ",
                  "state": "default",
                  "foreground": "foreground"
                },
                {
                  "text": "a stable identifier",
                  "state": "info",
                  "foreground": "accent"
                },
                {
                  "text": ", and let a small script resolve them at read time.",
                  "state": "default",
                  "foreground": "foreground"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "para-30",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "The lesson is the same one the archive teaches about itself:",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-31",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "keep the format boring, keep the structure explicit, and keep",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "para-32",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "default",
              "text": "a copy somewhere else. Everything else is a matter of taste.",
              "foreground": "foreground"
            },
            {
              "id": "meta-footer",
              "kind": "text",
              "state": "muted",
              "text": "Last updated 2026-08-13 · source: local notes",
              "foreground": "text-muted"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
